[[ ## document ## ]]
{
  "title": "CAM Reconciliation Dispute Documentation",
  "path": "engagements/stonebridge-partners/fy2025-pbc/cam-reconciliation-dispute-documentation.docx",
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "text": "CAM Reconciliation — Disputed Line Items Documentation"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Prepared by: Lucia Mendes, Senior Tax Accountant"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Prepared for: Evan Doyle (Stonebridge Partners), Gabriel Fontes (Stonebridge Partners)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Date: Friday, current week (per commitment made Tuesday)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Re: FY2025 PBC coordination — Common Area Maintenance (CAM) reconciliation, two disputed line items. This package sets out the exact dollar amounts, the underlying calculations, and the supporting basis for each position, resolving the open items for the FY2025 PBC file."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Disputed Line Item 1: Snow Removal & Ice Control — Contracted Services"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Disputed amount: $18,475.00"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Landlord's CAM claim: $18,475.00"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Stonebridge position (supported): $14,920.00"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Difference: $3,555.00"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Calculation and Basis"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The landlord included the full winter-season contract for snow removal and ice control across the entire property, including the retail pad buildings that are not part of Stonebridge's leased premises. The CAM reconciliation should allocate snow removal costs based on the ratio of Stonebridge's leasable area to the total leasable area of the property served by the contract."
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Item", "Amount / Factor"],
        "rows": [
          ["Total snow removal contract (season)", "$42,700.00"],
          ["Total leasable area served by contract (sq ft)", "185,000"],
          ["Stonebridge leasable area (sq ft)", "64,600"],
          ["Stonebridge pro-rata share", "64,600 / 185,000 = 34.92%"],
          ["Supportable snow removal allocation (34.92% × $42,700.00)", "$14,920.00"],
          ["Landlord's claimed amount", "$18,475.00"],
          ["Excess claimed (disputed)", "$3,555.00"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The landlord's claim of $18,475.00 corresponds to a 43.27% share (18,475 / 42,700), which does not match any documented area ratio. Supporting documentation: winter service contract dated 11/15/2024, property site plan, and lease Exhibit C (premises area schedule)."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Disputed Line Item 2: Parking Lot Sealcoating & Striping — Capital vs. Operating"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Disputed amount: $31,250.00"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Landlord's CAM claim: $31,250.00"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Stonebridge position (supported): $0.00 (capital item, not a recoverable CAM operating expense)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Difference: $31,250.00"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Calculation and Basis"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The invoice from the sealcoating contractor (dated 6/10/2025) describes full parking lot resurfacing including crack repair, new base coat application, and restriping across all 460 parking stalls. This is a betterment that extends the useful life of the parking lot surface by more than one year, and it is not a routine maintenance or repair expense. Under the lease, Section 6.2(b), 'CAM Operating Expenses' explicitly exclude 'capital improvements, replacements, or betterments.' The invoice total is $62,500.00; the landlord allocated 50% to Stonebridge's CAM, claiming $31,250.00."
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Item", "Amount / Factor"],
        "rows": [
          ["Total sealcoating invoice (6/10/2025)", "$62,500.00"],
          ["Landlord's CAM allocation percentage applied", "50%"],
          ["Landlord's claimed CAM amount", "$31,250.00"],
          ["Classification per lease Section 6.2(b)", "Capital betterment — excluded from CAM"],
          ["Recoverable amount", "$0.00"],
          ["Excess claimed (disputed)", "$31,250.00"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Supporting documentation: contractor invoice #SL-2291 dated 6/10/2025, lease Section 6.2(b) (CAM exclusions), and the property manager's capital project authorization form dated 5/28/2025, which classifies the work as 'parking lot capital renewal.'"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Summary of Disputed Amounts"
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Line Item", "Landlord Claim", "Stonebridge Position", "Difference"],
        "rows": [
          ["Snow Removal & Ice Control", "$18,475.00", "$14,920.00", "$3,555.00"],
          ["Parking Lot Sealcoating & Striping", "$31,250.00", "$0.00", "$31,250.00"],
          ["Total", "$49,725.00", "$14,920.00", "$34,805.00"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Total adjustment requested: $34,805.00 reduction to the FY2025 CAM charges."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Next Steps and Coordination"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "This documentation package is delivered per the commitment made on Tuesday. Once Evan and Gabriel confirm agreement with these positions, we will update the FY2025 PBC file and adjust the CAM accrual accordingly. The Q1/Q2 withholding detail has been settled and is available; Q3/Q4 split ownership remains locked per the earlier confirmation, and timing will follow the FY2025 PBC coordination schedule."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Please direct any questions or requested revisions to me by end of day Wednesday of next week so we can finalize the FY2025 PBC file before the working-session closeout."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Regards,\nLucia Mendes\nSenior Accountant, Tax\nStonebridge Partners engagement team"
      }
    ]
  }
}

